/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Time Time
 * @ingroup Foundation
 * @brief Clock abstractions and time utilities.
 *
 * Time models a monotonic tick source and the values derived from it. A Clock
 * binds a tick-reading function and a Frequency; `Now()` combines the current
 * Tick with the identity of that Clock in a TimePoint. Duration stores a count
 * of ticks, while Frequency and Period describe the scale of each tick.
 * `FOUNDATION_TIME` enables this complete family. Consumers choose which time
 * types to instantiate in source code; Clock, Duration, Frequency, Period,
 * Tick, and TimePoint are not separate CMake features.
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeHeaders Public Headers
 *
 * | Need | Header |
 * | ---- | ------ |
 * | Entire Foundation library | `#include <Foundation.h>` |
 * | Entire Time module | `#include <Foundation_Time.h>` |
 * | Nested module umbrella | `#include <Foundation/Time.h>` |
 * | One time type | `#include <Foundation/Time/<Type>.h>` |
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeTypes Public Types
 *
 * | Type | Meaning |
 * | ---- | ------- |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Tick "Tick" | Unsigned 32-bit counter value. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Frequency "Frequency" | Ticks per second as a ratio. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Period "Period" | Seconds per tick as a ratio. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Duration "Duration" | Number of elapsed ticks without clock identity. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_TimePoint "TimePoint" | Tick value associated with one Clock instance. |
 * | @ref Foundation_Time_Clock "Clock" | Callback-backed tick source and its frequency. |
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeUsage Basic Usage
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * Foundation::Time::Tick ReadTick();
 *
 * Foundation::Time::Clock clock(ReadTick, Foundation::Time::Frequency(1000, 1));
 *
 * const Foundation::Time::TimePoint start = clock.Now();
 * // Work performed here...
 * const Foundation::Time::TimePoint end = clock.Now();
 * const Foundation::Time::Duration elapsed = end - start;
 * const float milliseconds = elapsed.Milliseconds(clock.GetPeriod());
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeModel Model and Validity
 *
 * - Tick is `uint32_t`; arithmetic follows unsigned wraparound semantics.
 * - A default TimePoint has no Clock and `IsValid()` returns false.
 * - TimePoints compare as ordered only when they reference the same Clock
 *   instance. Subtracting points from different clocks returns zero Duration.
 * - TimePoint stores a non-owning Clock pointer; the Clock must outlive every
 *   point that retains its identity.
 * - Frequency and Period are backed by Math::Ratio. A zero denominator is
 *   invalid and conversion methods return the behavior documented by each type.
 * - Duration conversion requires the Period belonging to the relevant Clock.
 *
 * @warning Wraparound, cross-clock arithmetic, zero-frequency reciprocal
 * behavior, and raw Clock identity remain pre-1.0 decisions under `API-011` in
 * @ref Foundation_Workflows_PublicApiAudit.
 *
 * @section FoundationTimeExamples Runnable Examples
 *
 * The examples `Foundation_Time_Frequency`, `Foundation_Time_Period`, and
 * `Foundation_Time_ClockAndDuration` demonstrate construction, conversion,
 * mutation, clock identity, arithmetic, and units. See
 * @ref Foundation_Examples "Examples" for build and launch instructions.
 */

/**
 * @namespace Foundation::Time
 * @ingroup Foundation_Time
 * @brief Tick sources, time values, and unit conversions.
 */

